      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): add timeout to guardedJsonApiRequest",
        "body": "<!--\nRelated: PR #102865 (same hardening pattern for provider voices-list timeouts)\n-->\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where voice-call providers (Twilio, Plivo, Telnyx) could hang indefinitely when their JSON API control endpoints accept the connection but never respond, because the shared `guardedJsonApiRequest` helper did not pass any timeout to the SSRF-guarded fetch.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a bounded default timeout of 30 seconds to the shared helper and expose an optional `timeoutMs` override for callers that need different limits. The default matches the voices-list timeout pattern used in recent provider hardening PRs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nVoice-call control requests now fail fast with a timeout error instead of blocking the provider when a remote API is unreachable or stalls, improving reliability for outbound calls and status checks.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused unit + loopback tests pass:\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/voice-call/src/providers/shared/guarded-json-api.test.ts extensions/voice-call/src/providers/shared/guarded-json-api.loopback.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 2 test files passed, 8 tests passed.\n",
        "branch": "fix/voice-call-guarded-json-api-timeout",
